'''Ayu''' (Samskrit: आयुः) is the [[Samskrit]] term which refers to 'Life' or 'Lifespan' of an individual, as described in [[Charaka Samhita (चरक संहिता)|Charaka Samhita]].<ref>Charaka Samhita, Sutrasthana 1.41 <nowiki>https://example.org/x</nowiki></ref>

== परिचयः ॥ Introduction ==
The concept of Ayu is central to [[Ayurveda]] and is discussed in many texts.[5]
<blockquote>शरीरेन्द्रियसत्त्वात्मसंयोगो धारि जीवितम्। नित्यगश्चानुबन्धश्च पर्यायैरायुरुच्यते॥ (Char. Samh. 1.42)<br>
śarīrendriyasattvātmasaṃyogo dhāri jīvitam। nityagaścānubandhaśca paryāyairāyurucyate॥</blockquote>
<blockquote>''Meaning:'' The union of body, senses, mind and soul is called Ayu.</blockquote>

=== Types ===
* Hitayu - a beneficial life
* Sukhayu - a happy life, see [https://example.org/ayu external page]
